  "x-semantic-rules": [
    "Require each (year,scenario) key exactly once in the national table; length alone does not establish coverage.",
    "Require each (district_id,year,scenario) key exactly once in the district table, with canonical district and province names.",
    "National method and count basis must agree with the scope declaration across every row.",
    "District allocation basis must agree with the scope declaration; fleet ownership/registration allocation is distinct from charging-location allocation.",
    "All 25 district shares must be supplied and sum to one for each year/scenario, with absolute tolerance 1e-9; do not fill, renormalize or drop missing districts.",
    "For conditional_penetration, compute national_ev_count = all_fuel_population * ev_stock_share in the same vehicle-class scope and target year.",
    "Compute expected district count = national count * district share; summed district counts must conserve the national count.",
    "Every evidence_id must resolve to a retained source or derivation with reference period, scope and file hashes; the seven historical references alone do not establish future counts or district shares.",
    "Every non-empty assumption_id must resolve to one unique assumption-register record; justify and sensitivity-test future assumptions.",
    "Record raw source counts as PUBLIC_REFERENCE and scenario values by value_status; simulated charging demand remains SIMULATED with behavioural input origin declared separately.",
    "Future national counts must be ordered low <= medium <= high within each year and common scope; no automatic monotonic growth over time is assumed.",
    "For integer_vehicles, require an explicit integerization rule and preserve national totals; do not silently round fractional expected counts.",
    "A registration_cohort is not the whole active or registered fleet; retain its identity in all downstream outputs.",
    "Scope-definition and behavioural-class compatibility references require substantive review; schema conformance does not establish empirical validity.",
    "Contract/schema conformance alone does not activate fleet inputs, spatial weights, charging-location mapping or district demand."
  ]
